From 40eacc9a278738ba3fce5d4f1b030e543b4ca2e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <virajslko@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:19:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] render: leave out an image effect that can't be built,
 not the image
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Workshop scene can ship its own (older) copy of an effect's shader in its
scene.pkg. When that copy doesn't compile here (2189783622's godrays
fragment uses v_Bounds, which its vertex stage never declares), the CPass
constructor throws, CImage::setup unwinds, and CScene drops the whole
object ("Failed to setup object 13"). For a scene whose background is that
one image the wallpaper renders black; elsewhere a layer silently goes
missing.

CImage::setup now builds each effect's passes inside its own try block: if
any pass of an effect throws, the passes that effect already added are
deleted and the image goes on with its other effects, logging
"Leaving out effect <id> (<name>) of object <id>: <reason>". Wallpaper
Engine shows the image in that case too (at worst without the effect).

Not for a passthrough or fullscreen layer (composelayer / fullscreenlayer
models): those exist only to post-process what is below them, and part of
their effect chain is an arbitrary picture — 3432999904's fullscreen layer
with its tone_mapping effect left out covered the whole scene in black. A
failing effect still drops such a layer whole, as before.

Origin: ours
Why: one broken packaged effect blanked a whole scene in lp-player (scene corpus: 2189783622) and dropped image layers of others (3233141951, 3326873240, 3354740764)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
index a5586cd..062c7b5 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
@@ -647,7 +647,12 @@ void CImage::setup () {
 	    auto endEffect = cur->effect->passes.end ();
 	    auto curOverride = cur->passOverrides.begin ();
 	    auto endOverride = cur->passOverrides.end ();
+	    // an effect whose pass can't be built (a packaged shader that doesn't compile, a missing material) is
+	    // left out on its own: the image still renders, without it — not dropped with the whole object
+	    // (except a passthrough/fullscreen layer, below)
+	    const auto passesBefore = this->m_passes.size ();
 
+	    try {
 	    for (; curEffect != endEffect; ++curEffect) {
 		if (!(*curEffect)->material.has_value ()) {
 		    if (!(*curEffect)->command.has_value ()) {
@@ -705,6 +710,20 @@ void CImage::setup () {
 		    }
 		}
 	    }
+	    } catch (const std::exception& e) {
+		// a passthrough/fullscreen layer exists only to post-process what's below it: part of its effect
+		// chain is an arbitrary picture (measured: a black screen over 3432999904), so it still goes whole
+		if (this->m_image.model->passthrough || this->m_image.model->fullscreen) {
+		    throw;
+		}
+
+		sLog.error ("Leaving out effect ", cur->id, " (", cur->name, ") of object ", this->m_image.id, ": ", e.what ());
+
+		while (this->m_passes.size () > passesBefore) {
+		    delete this->m_passes.back ();
+		    this->m_passes.pop_back ();
+		}
+	    }
 	}
     }
 
